rem Sphere Packing
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=222
rem Find the shortest tube of radius R
rem that holds spheres of every integer
rem radius from Lo to Hi, in thousandths

use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

option R integer = 50
option Lo integer = 30
option Hi integer = 50

rem Neighbouring spheres touch the tube
rem on opposite sides, 2 sqrt(R (a + b -
rem R)) apart along its axis. The best
rem order puts every second sphere from
rem the largest down, then the rest back
rem up: the smallest sit in the middle.
Rs = Hi to Lo by -1 array
Pos' = 0 till (Rs len)
Even = Pos mod 2 equal 0
Down' = Rs filter Even
Rest' = Rs filter (not Even)
Order = concat Down (Rest reverse)
N = Order len
A' = Order take (N - 1)
B' = Order drop 1
Gap' = 2 * ((R * (A + B - R)) sqrt)
Ends = Order 0 + Order (N - 1)
Length = Ends + (Gap sum)
Answer = Length * 1000 round 0
Answer print
